  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "6656504",
      "title": "Reactive: Syncing HTML and Form",
      "lectureOrder": 529,
      "videoOrder": 485,
      "sourceHash": "9d73e69735fe5b4b05937b6ef4516671e577e9d242a25878e7c20a22c6cfbea4",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.52,
          "end": 3.48,
          "en": "In the last lecture,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.48,
          "end": 5.79,
          "en": "we created our form here in TypeScript.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.79,
          "end": 8.052,
          "en": "The issue is, it's nice to have it here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.052,
          "end": 10.44,
          "en": "but our actual form, you could say,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 10.44,
          "end": 13.2,
          "en": "lives in the HTML template.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 13.2,
          "end": 17.34,
          "en": "So we somehow need to synchronize our HTML inputs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 17.34,
          "end": 21.54,
          "en": "and our own form, or this form in general with our own form.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 21.54,
          "end": 23.61,
          "en": "Right now, Angular doesn't know",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 23.61,
          "end": 27.15,
          "en": "which of our TypeScript controls here relates",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 27.15,
          "end": 29.61,
          "en": "to which input in our template code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 29.61,
          "end": 32.117,
          "en": "It actually doesn't even know that our form,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 32.117,
          "end": 35.85,
          "en": "signup form here, should be attached to this form.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 35.85,
          "end": 38.25,
          "en": "Right now, the one thing it is doing is,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 38.25,
          "end": 40.65,
          "en": "it is auto-detecting that this is a form",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 40.65,
          "end": 42.72,
          "en": "and it creates a form for us.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 42.72,
          "end": 44.85,
          "en": "Now we don't want it to do that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 44.85,
          "end": 47.25,
          "en": "so we have to add some directives",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 47.25,
          "end": 48.87,
          "en": "to override this default behavior",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 48.87,
          "end": 52.44,
          "en": "to give Angular different instructions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 52.44,
          "end": 54.03,
          "en": "For these directives to work,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 54.03,
          "end": 55.83,
          "en": "you definitely need to make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 55.83,
          "end": 59.37,
          "en": "that you add the import to the reactive forms module",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 59.37,
          "end": 60.6,
          "en": "in your app module,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 60.6,
          "end": 63.21,
          "en": "otherwise you will get errors.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 63.21,
          "end": 65.76,
          "en": "Now, the first directive we need to add",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 65.76,
          "end": 68.37,
          "en": "is here on the form itself,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 68.37,
          "end": 70.05,
          "en": "via property binding,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 70.05,
          "end": 72.603,
          "en": "the form group directive.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 73.44,
          "end": 75.247,
          "en": "Now this simply tells Angular,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 75.247,
          "end": 77.64,
          "en": "\"Hey please take my form group.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 77.64,
          "end": 78.93,
          "en": "Don't infer one.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 78.93,
          "end": 80.94,
          "en": "Don't create a form for me.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 80.94,
          "end": 82.86,
          "en": "Use my form group.\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 82.86,
          "end": 85.17,
          "en": "And we need to set up property binding here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 85.17,
          "end": 87.48,
          "en": "because we need to pass our form",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 87.48,
          "end": 89.61,
          "en": "as an argument to the directive.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 89.61,
          "end": 93,
          "en": "So here we should reference our signup form,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 93,
          "end": 94.89,
          "en": "the property we created here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 94.89,
          "end": 96.72,
          "en": "which stores our form.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 96.72,
          "end": 99.93,
          "en": "We're passing this via property binding to the form group,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 99.93,
          "end": 103.28999999999999,
          "en": "and now this form is actually synchronized",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 103.28999999999999,
          "end": 105.57,
          "en": "with the form we created in TypeScript.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 105.57,
          "end": 108.84,
          "en": "But we still need to tell Angular which controls",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 108.84,
          "end": 112.68,
          "en": "should be connected to which inputs in the template code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 112.68,
          "end": 115.59,
          "en": "For this, we get a number directive.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 115.59,
          "end": 118.95,
          "en": "On this input here, for example, the username,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 118.95,
          "end": 122.16,
          "en": "we add the form control",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 122.16,
          "end": 124.29,
          "en": "name directive",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 124.29,
          "end": 127.95,
          "en": "to tell Angular, \"hey what's the name of this input",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 127.95,
          "end": 130.71,
          "en": "in my form, in my TypeScript form?\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 130.71,
          "end": 133.86,
          "en": "Well, the name is \"username,\" this name here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 133.86,
          "end": 136.8,
          "en": "because that's the control I want to connect to this input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 136.8,
          "end": 139.32,
          "en": "So I simply pass username here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 139.32,
          "end": 142.65,
          "en": "If you're wondering why I'm not using property binding,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 142.65,
          "end": 144.72,
          "en": "I'm passing a string here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 144.72,
          "end": 146.61,
          "en": "So if you want to use property binding,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 146.61,
          "end": 149.76,
          "en": "you can do this by wrapping this in square brackets",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 149.76,
          "end": 152.88,
          "en": "and then enclosing username in single quotation marks.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 152.88,
          "end": 156.24,
          "en": "Otherwise, it would search for a property named username.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 156.24,
          "end": 158.43,
          "en": "But this is overly complicated.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 158.43,
          "end": 160.17000000000002,
          "en": "If you just want to pass a string,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 160.17000000000002,
          "end": 163.86,
          "en": "simply omit the square brackets and you're good to go.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 163.86,
          "end": 165.337,
          "en": "So if this were telling Angular,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 165.337,
          "end": 169.26,
          "en": "\"Hey, my form should be connected to the form stored",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 169.26,
          "end": 170.95499999999998,
          "en": "in the sign-up form property,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 170.95499999999998,
          "end": 174,
          "en": "and in this form, this input here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 174,
          "end": 177.36,
          "en": "should be connected to the control with the name username.\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 177.36,
          "end": 181.05,
          "en": "Well, now I can simply repeat this for the email,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 181.05,
          "end": 184.74,
          "en": "here the name was \"email,\" the name we set up here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 184.74,
          "end": 187.35,
          "en": "Now this control is connected",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 187.35,
          "end": 189.51,
          "en": "and for the gender, of course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 189.51,
          "end": 193.638,
          "en": "So in this input here, I will bind this to gender.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 193.638,
          "end": 195,
          "en": "Now if this...",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 195,
          "end": 197.142,
          "en": "let's save this, so that it compiles,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 197.142,
          "end": 200.07,
          "en": "and now let's have a look at it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 200.07,
          "end": 202.47,
          "en": "We don't see any errors, which looks good.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 202.47,
          "end": 204.75,
          "en": "We see that mail is pre-selected.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 204.75,
          "end": 207.72,
          "en": "Looks promising, because that was the default value we set",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 207.72,
          "end": 209.91,
          "en": "when we created the control in TypeScript.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 209.91,
          "end": 211.82999999999998,
          "en": "And if I now switch to female,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 211.82999999999998,
          "end": 213.75,
          "en": "only one of the two is selected.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 213.75,
          "end": 216.93,
          "en": "We also see that if we select email here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 216.93,
          "end": 219.3,
          "en": "that the Angular classes are attached,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 219.3,
          "end": 221.79,
          "en": "untouched, pristine, valid, and so on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 221.79,
          "end": 225.36,
          "en": "So it indeed looks like our inputs in HTML",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 225.36,
          "end": 227.22,
          "en": "are correctly synchronized",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 227.22,
          "end": 229.8,
          "en": "to our form we created in TypeScript.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 229.8,
          "end": 231.51,
          "en": "So this was successful.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 231.51,
          "end": 234.32999999999998,
          "en": "The next step is to actually submit the form",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 234.32999999999998,
          "end": 235.893,
          "en": "to see how this works.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
